1
00:00:00,275 --> 00:00:04,646
A Foley catheter is a dual-channel tube for continuous bladder drainage.

2
00:00:05,175 --> 00:00:09,781
Inside its soft silicone shaft, two separate channels work independently side by side.

3
00:00:10,375 --> 00:00:14,793
During placement, the rounded tip glides smoothly until its top eyes enter the bladder.

4
00:00:15,375 --> 00:00:20,310
Ten milliliters of sterile water inflate a tiny balloon at the neck, gently anchoring it.

5
00:00:20,975 --> 00:00:25,675
Gravity drains urine through the top ports into a closed sterile bag without backflow.

6
00:00:26,225 --> 00:00:29,656
Deflating the valve collapses the balloon for smooth removal.
